# ouroboros#156: `what is s at L` through a spliced module call. The VM
# stamps g_trace_current_line with whatever line last EXECUTED -- inside the
# callee, its return line -- which retires earlier same-line history
# entries; the AOT stamped only traced statements' own lines, so the
# spliced callee never restamped and the query answered seed! where the
# VM answers seed!!!. Since round 140 every statement stamps, the callee
# included, and the two agree.
import _am156
s is "seed"
s is _am156.tag of s
s is _am156.tag of s
s is _am156.tag of s
print of (what is s at 4)
print of (prev of s)
